**English (preserving the poetic rhythm)**  

Spring has come;  
Flowers burst open;  
Mountains turn verdant;  
Waters grow greener;  
Wind warms;  
Clouds thin;  
Birds sing merrily;  
Butterflies dance;  
Bees bustle;  
All living things revive;  
Earth a scene of vibrant life.  

People step out,  
Feeling the breath of spring.  
Children race and laugh across the fields;  
Elders sit beneath the trees, playing chess and chatting;  
Everywhere brims with hope and joy.  



**Japanese (keeping a lyrical cadence)**  

春が来た  
花が開く  
山は青く  
水はいっそう緑に  
風
